  "chapter": {
    "number": 110,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(111) Alleluia."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will give you thanks, O Lord, with my whole heart, in the council of the upright, and in the congregation.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The works of the Lord are great, sought out",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 209
          },
          {
            "text": "according to all his will.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "His work is worthy of thanksgiving and honor: and his righteousness endures for ever and ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He has caused his wonderful works to be remembered: the Lord is merciful and compassionate.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He has given food to them that fear him: he will remember his covenant for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He has declared to his people the power of his works, to give them the inheritance of the heathen.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The works of his hands are truth and judgment: all his commandments are sure:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "established for ever and ever, done in truth and uprightness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He sent redemption to his people: he commanded his covenant for ever: holy and fearful is his name.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The fear of the Lord is the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 210
          },
          {
            "text": "beginning of wisdom, and all that act accordingly have a good understanding; his praise endures for ever and ever.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 209,
